                            [object_id] => 2757
                            [sightseeing_name] => Cochin - Munnar (via Athriapilly)
                            [sightseeing_description] => Starting from Cochin, you'll be driven approximately 70 km (about 2-2.5 hours) to Athirapilly, where you'll visit the majestic Athirapilly Waterfalls, known as the "Niagara of India," and the nearby Vazhachal Waterfalls, both surrounded by lush forests and perfect for photography. 
Note : Visiting Time at Athirapilly :  09:00 AM  to 04 : 00 PM
After exploring these natural wonders, you'll continue on a scenic 150 km (around 4-5 hours) drive to Munnar,  taking time along the way to appreciate the beautiful Valara Waterfall and Cheeyappara Waterfalls, among others. stopping en route at attractions like scenic spice plantations and picturesque viewpoints offering stunning views of rolling hills and tea estate.  As you continue your journey to Munnar, you will check into your hotel upon arrival. After checking in, the rest of the day is yours to enjoy at your leisure. Have a delightful overnight stay at the hotel.

